<title>USA: Photocomm Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Photocomm Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>UNAUDITED RESULTS			   Fiscal First Quarter</p>
<p>							Ended November 30</p>
<p>							1996	    1995</p>
<p> Sales revenues			   $7,556,692     $5,281,273</p>
<p> Cost of sales			     5,400,841	3,947,599</p>
<p> Gross profit				2,155,851	1,333,674</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses		1,750,335	1,106,279</p>
<p> Operating profit (loss)		   405,516	  227,395</p>
<p> Interest income (expense)		(48,844)	 (17,624)</p>
<p> Other income (expense)			6,463	   10,010</p>
<p> Net income before tax		     363,135	  219,781</p>
<p> Benefit from tax loss carryforward*    90,000		 --</p>
<p> Net income				    453,135	  219,781</p>
<p> Earnings per common share		    0.03	     0.01</p>
<p>* The Company continued to recognize benefit from its tax loss carryforward consistent with fiscal 1996.  The 1996 valuation allowance adjustment was recognized after three consecutive years of profitability, and the Company anticipates recognizing on a quarterly basis.  The adjustment will be reevaluated on an on-going basis based upon generation of future taxable income.</p>
<p>Photocomm, Inc., headquartered in Scottsdale, Arizona, is the nation's largest publicly-owned manufacturer and marketer of wireless solar electric power systems.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
